_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 2
---
order: 2
---
short_label: VI.2
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If a straight line is drawn parallel to one of the sides of a triangle, then it cuts the sides of the triangle proportionally; and, if the sides of the triangle are cut proportionally, then the line joining the points of section is parallel to the remaining side of the triangle.
----
proof:

Let {DE} be drawn parallel to {BC}, one of the sides of the triangle {ABC}.

I say that {BD} is to {AD} as {CE} is to {AE}.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="290" height="300" tabindex="0"></canvas>
