              highlighted: ["DE","BC"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "equal triangles on the same base are in the same parallels", ref: "I.39" }] },
            { text: "Therefore, if a straight line is drawn parallel to one of the sides of a triangle,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DE","BC"] },
            { text: "then it cuts the sides of the triangle proportionally;",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BD","AD","CE","AE"] },
            { text: "and, if the sides of the triangle are cut proportionally,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BD","AD","CE","AE"] },
            { text: "then the line joining the points of section is parallel to the remaining side of the triangle.",
